Vulnerability Title

Verbose Error Message and Stack Trace Disclosure

Vulnerability Category
Information Disclosure
Improper Error Handling
Sensitive Information Exposure
OWASP Top 10 Category (2021/2025 Mapping)
A05:2021 – Security Misconfiguration
A09:2021 – Security Logging and Monitoring Failures (secondary mapping)
CVSS v3.1 Score
5.3 – Medium
CVSS Vector
CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:L/I:N/A:N
Description

The application exposes detailed internal exception information and full stack traces in HTTP responses when an error occurs.

During testing, the application disclosed sensitive backend implementation details including:

Java class names
Package structure
Internal method names
Line numbers
Framework details
Database technology references
JDBC implementation details
Internal service architecture

Example exposed components observed:

ReferenceDataHandler.java
SoapReferenceDataService
JdbcTemplate
SybPreparedStatement
Apache CXF
Spring Framework
Sybase JDBC

The application returned raw exception data directly to the client instead of a generic error response.

Impact

Verbose error messages may help attackers perform targeted attacks by revealing sensitive internal information such as:

Backend technologies in use
Application architecture
Internal API/service flow
Database technologies
Source code structure
File names and line numbers
Framework versions/components

This information can significantly aid attackers in:

Reconnaissance
Vulnerability research
Crafting targeted exploits
Identifying attack surfaces
Technology fingerprinting
Mitigation

Implement secure exception handling and avoid exposing internal errors to end users.

Recommended Controls

Return generic user-friendly error messages:

“An unexpected error occurred.”
Disable stack trace exposure in production environments.
Configure centralized exception handling.
Log detailed errors only on the server-side.
Remove:
File paths
Line numbers
SQL errors
Framework details
Stack traces
Implement custom error pages/API responses.
Review application debug configurations before deployment.
